    "answer_html": "<p><strong>Answer:</strong> (A) 2/3 and 7⅓ — Let the sequence be -6, A₁, A₂, 14. Here n = 4, first term a = -6, last term t₄ = 14. Thus 14 = -6 + 3d ⇒ 3d = 20 ⇒ d = 20/3. First A.M. A₁ = -6 + 20/3 = 2/3. Second A.M. A₂ = 2/3 + 20/3 = 22/3 = 7⅓.</p>",
